# Direct links from any platform

- Use `public/link_policy.json` as the editable source of truth. Add platforms
  there, not in code.
- Any employer domain is allowed. Allow-listed platforms (LinkedIn, Indeed,
  Naukri, FreeJobAlert, Foundit, Shine, TimesJobs, Internshala, Apna and peers)
  are allowed when the URL points at one specific job/notice page.
- Do not fetch or scrape LinkedIn, Indeed or Naukri. Validate their URL
  patterns only. 403, 429, 999, timeouts and TLS errors are UNKNOWN → keep.
- Remove only DEAD links (404/410, confirmed soft-404, closed/expired text).
  Never delete data: archive it.
- Home pages, search/listing pages and section roots are NOT_DIRECT → publish
  in "Careers portals", not as individual jobs.
- Resolve news wrappers and shorteners first; drop only if unresolvable. Strip
  tracking parameters.
- `apply_url` must come from the source/candidate, never the LLM. Blank invented
  fields instead of generating them.
- Front end: "Apply" / "Apply on <platform>" + hostname,
  `rel="noopener noreferrer"`; "Report a broken link" stays; archived records
  render no outbound link.
- Keep SSRF checks and certificate verification on. `verify=False` is
  forbidden.
- Before committing: `py -m pytest tests -q`, `py scripts/link_guard.py`.
  Before deploying: `npm run build` then `py scripts/link_guard.py --dist dist`.
- Full policy: `docs/LINK_POLICY.md`.
